WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.859
(pleasant music)

00:00:02.859 --> 00:00:04.765
- [Narrator] The marshy
region in the south of France

00:00:04.765 --> 00:00:07.437
is home to herds of white Camargue horses,

00:00:07.437 --> 00:00:11.144
one of the oldest and rarest
horse breeds in the world.

00:00:11.144 --> 00:00:13.539
Since the 1500s, the people of Camargue

00:00:13.539 --> 00:00:17.706
have upheld a tradition
dedicated to caring for them.

00:00:24.296 --> 00:00:27.213
(foreign language)

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:44.737
For centuries, there has
been unwavering respect

00:00:44.737 --> 00:00:47.337
and devotion to the Camargue horses.

00:00:47.337 --> 00:00:49.455
They appear in artwork, cave paintings,

00:00:49.455 --> 00:00:53.139
and have long been inspiration
for the people of the region.

00:00:53.139 --> 00:00:55.413
However, in recent years the population

00:00:55.413 --> 00:00:58.437
is no longer as strong as it once once.

00:00:58.437 --> 00:01:01.354
(foreign language)

00:01:10.106 --> 00:01:11.973
Every day, Marie and other guardians

00:01:11.973 --> 00:01:15.382
feed, groom, and work
their horses on the land.

00:01:15.382 --> 00:01:18.299
(foreign language)

00:01:20.754 --> 00:01:22.545
Despite all the guardians' hard work,

00:01:22.545 --> 00:01:24.305
for them it is worth it.

00:01:24.305 --> 00:01:26.494
The Camargue horses are
unequivocally intertwined

00:01:26.494 --> 00:01:28.955
with their regional identity.

00:01:28.955 --> 00:01:31.253
To uphold the tradition
that keeps the breed alive

00:01:31.253 --> 00:01:33.392
is the genesis of their passion.

00:01:33.392 --> 00:01:36.392
(foreign language)

